<pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="Ia407fb5022f804779d6320aa44042badc72a3d9a" commit="4506b75c1d331f4c00dbf7ddd44628aededa28ee" commit_message="UPSTREAM: chromeos: vboot and chromeos dependency removal for sw write protect state  This removes the dependency on chromeos and vboot for the sw write protect state function: vboot_get_sw_write_protect, renamed to get_sw_write_protect_state to both reflect this change and become consistent with the definition of get_write_protect_state that is already in use.  Original-Change-Id: I47ce31530a03f6749e0f370e5d868466318b3bb6 Original-Signed-off-by: Paul Kocialkowski &lt;contact@paulk.fr&gt; Original-Reviewed-on: http://review.coreboot.org/11496 Original-Tested-by: build bot (Jenkins) Original-Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:44827 BRANCH=None TEST=Built and booted glados.  Change-Id: Ia407fb5022f804779d6320aa44042badc72a3d9a Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/303330 Reviewed-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="303330" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/30/303330/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="Ic1a94d95dae7dc4ff960fbb2de4b7e7fbb7bd639" commit="edf00479497f0f010663398e1a223553a1c82124" commit_message="UPSTREAM: chromeos: vboot-related functions move to common vboot code  This moves a few vboot-prefixed functions that were defined in chromeos.c to vboot_common.c, since those are only relevant to vboot and depend on the vboot handoff data. This allows more separation between CONFIG_CHROMEOS and what CONFIG_CHROMEOS selects, so that each separate option (such as CONFIG_VBOOT_VERIFY_FIRMWARE) can be enabled separately.  Thus, the actual definitions of these functions will only be declared when CONFIG_VBOOT_VERIFY_FIRMWARE is set, so the check before calling vboot_skip_display_init in bootmode was also adapted.  Original-Change-Id: I52f8a408645566dac0a2100e819c8ed5d3d88ea5 Original-Signed-off-by: Paul Kocialkowski &lt;contact@paulk.fr&gt; Original-Reviewed-on: http://review.coreboot.org/11497 Original-Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Original-Tested-by: build bot (Jenkins) Original-Reviewed-by: Paul Menzel &lt;paulepanter@users.sourceforge.net&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:44827 BRANCH=None TEST=Built and booted glados.  Change-Id: Ic1a94d95dae7dc4ff960fbb2de4b7e7fbb7bd639 Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/303331 Reviewed-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="303331" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/31/303331/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="If71c8892fd3d8dbe9b39c296cbf17143df6d9fa5" commit="5039b92a1454ad12277395f677453b028f654fd4" commit_message="UPSTREAM: x86: provide common macro for linking early stages  In order to support verstage on x86 one needs to link verstage like romstage since it needs all the cache-as-ram goodies. Therefore, provide a macro that one can invoke that provides the necessary recipes for linking that particular stage in such an environment.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:44827 BRANCH=None TEST=Built and booted glados.  Original-Change-Id: I12f4872df09fff6715829de68fc374e230350c2e Original-Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Original-Reviewed-on: http://review.coreboot.org/11739 Original-Tested-by: build bot (Jenkins) Original-Reviewed-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@google.com&gt;  Change-Id: If71c8892fd3d8dbe9b39c296cbf17143df6d9fa5 Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/303332 Reviewed-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="303332" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/32/303332/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I15e9f6b0c632ee5a2369da0709535d6cb0d94f61" commit="0b7ca52c9d28e9c1b387d1851fd8634c53a7595d" commit_message="UPSTREAM: x86: prepare cache-as-ram to allow multiple stages  In order to do a verification of romstage on x86 one needs to run verstage which verifies romstage (and the memory init code). However, x86 doesn't have SRAM like every other modern SoC so managing the cache-as-ram region is especially critical.  First move all of the &quot;shared&quot; objects to the beginning of the .car.data section. This change then ensures that each stage using car.ld to link has the same consistent view of the addresses of these fixed-sized objects in cache-as-ram. The CAR_GLOBALs can be unique per stage. However, these variables are expected to have a value of zero at the start of each stage. In order to allow a stage to provide those semantics outside of the initial cache-as-arm setup routine add _car_global_start and _car_global_end symbols. Those symbols can be used to clear the CAR_GLOBALs for that stage.  Note that the timestamp region can't be moved out similarly to the pre-ram cbmem console because the object storage of the timestamp cache is used *after* cache-as-ram is torn down to indicate if the cache should be used or not. Therefore, that timestamp needs to migrated to ram. A logic change in src/lib/timestamp.c could alleviate this requirement, but that task wasn't tackled in this patch.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:44827 BRANCH=None TEST=Built and booted glados.  Original-Change-Id: I15e9f6b0c632ee5a2369da0709535d6cb0d94f61 Original-Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Original-Reviewed-on: http://review.coreboot.org/11740 Original-Tested-by: build bot (Jenkins) Original-Reviewed-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@google.com&gt;  Change-Id: I15e9f6b0c632ee5a2369da0709535d6cb0d94f61 Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/302480 Reviewed-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="302480" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/80/302480/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="Ie3bbdd94d9c680357e8491acce26ad51fe19175c" commit="5f8333aed477407b4f994053288a1b544bab90eb" commit_message="BACKPORT: ASoC: rt5645: Add dmi for Broadwell  Add DMI data for Buddy project.  Signed-off-by: Bard Liao &lt;bardliao@realtek.com&gt; Signed-off-by: John Lin &lt;john.lin@realtek.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Brown &lt;broonie@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit e9159e7577cfd1ac8b3c5ea8916ad37bcd87e629) Signed-off-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt;  Conflicts:  sound/soc/codecs/rt5645.c - context fix  BUG=chrome-os-partner:43037 TEST=4ch recording on Buddy with TDM  Change-Id: Ie3bbdd94d9c680357e8491acce26ad51fe19175c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/300603 Commit-Ready: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="300603" owner_email="benzh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/03/300603/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I2b834ce393465946286a729a4f289221885901ef" commit="a6b926d4de3faaff0b57e32f0a7635f65d45726f" commit_message="BACKPORT: ASoC: rt5645: Add jd_invert for Broadwell  Broadwell can not triger the IRQ falling and rising simultaneously, so it can not detect jack-in and jack-out simultaneously. We add a flag &quot;jd_invert&quot; to platform data. If this flag is set, codec IRQ will be set to invert that forces IRQ as pulse when jack-in and jack-out.  Signed-off-by: John Lin &lt;john.lin@realtek.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Bard Liao &lt;bardliao@realtek.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Brown &lt;broonie@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 917536aeb88d34e06c1353b0dd144f0987bb66bd) Signed-off-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt;  Conflicts:  sound/soc/codecs/rt5645.c - context fix  BUG=chrome-os-partner:43037 TEST=4ch recording on Buddy with TDM  Change-Id: I2b834ce393465946286a729a4f289221885901ef Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/300604 Commit-Ready: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="300604" owner_email="benzh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/04/300604/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I420fd5ab729524ab95e3fd1850a678d1ac5dd85a" commit="17fb2cea4536a4c5bda0ed35edf9b92d3a66698a" commit_message="Fix syntax error.  BUG=None TEST=None  Change-Id: I420fd5ab729524ab95e3fd1850a678d1ac5dd85a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/303128 Commit-Ready: Kalin Stoyanov &lt;kalin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kalin Stoyanov &lt;kalin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shrawan Jha &lt;shrawan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="303128" owner_email="kalin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/28/303128/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iab993e96713996d51264fd5571a2d80ea4bb5095" commit="c6c31df337bd94fb5ed6ced9cf1f4c3c7b38c64e" commit_message="servo V2: Add uart controls for atmega.  BUG=none TEST=manual, servod still launches.  Can read &amp; write things like baudrate, stop bits, parity.    dut-control `dut-control -i | grep ^atmega | cut -d ' ' -f 1`   atmega_baudrate:115200   atmega_bits:eight   atmega_parity:none   atmega_pty:/dev/pts/42   atmega_rst:on   atmega_sbits:one  Change-Id: Iab993e96713996d51264fd5571a2d80ea4bb5095 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/303188 Commit-Ready: Todd Broch &lt;tbroch@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Todd Broch &lt;tbroch@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Nick Sanders &lt;nsanders@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="303188" owner_email="tbroch@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/hdctools" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/hdctools" ref="refs/changes/88/303188/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib986c721a8b0c8836940ac17ea73524bafa30972" commit="04e39ba2f70b529fae44526be6804b48173996c6" commit_message="chromeos-fonts: fallback to qemu for native runs  If the native chroot failed, try running it through qemu.  When the target code is built for the target board, it might use insns that are not usable on the build system.  We can't do this all the time as qemu is much slower than native runs (like 40seconds vs 15seconds).  BUG=chromium:473900 TEST=`emerge-samus chromeos-fonts` still works  Change-Id: Ib986c721a8b0c8836940ac17ea73524bafa30972 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/294923 Commit-Ready: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Jungshik Shin &lt;jshin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="294923" owner_email="vapier@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/23/294923/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ifb336420a1cec4f8795d889de05dc6354a53a87c" commit="ec172b99706fef4a0c98aab21677d1bb7085ff57" commit_message="Check total number of audio devices in shutdown test  Sometimes codec is missing after boot. Add a test to check audio codec is enumerated every time after boot.  BUG=chromium:532991 TEST=Manually test in my DUT  Change-Id: Ifb336420a1cec4f8795d889de05dc6354a53a87c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/302215 Commit-Ready: Hsu Wei-Cheng &lt;mojahsu@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hsu Wei-Cheng &lt;mojahsu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="302215" owner_email="mojahsu@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/15/302215/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I1333105c1c1fdeba1b6d2afe0d68e2b5b26bf85d" commit="de584ddb4993b55c9b07612ed733c455f2daaf3e" commit_message="UPSTREAM: lockdep: Fix the module unload key range freeing logic  Module unload calls lockdep_free_key_range(), which removes entries from the data structures. Most of the lockdep code OTOH assumes the data structures are append only; in specific see the comments in add_lock_to_list() and look_up_lock_class().  Clearly this has only worked by accident; make it work proper. The actual scenario to make it go boom would involve the memory freed by the module unlock being re-allocated and re-used for a lock inside of a rcu-sched grace period. This is a very unlikely scenario, still better plug the hole.  Use RCU list iteration in all places and ammend the comments.  Change lockdep_free_key_range() to issue a sync_sched() between removal from the lists and returning -- which results in the memory being freed. Further ensure the callers are placed correctly and comment the requirements.  Signed-off-by: Peter Zijlstra (Intel) &lt;peterz@infradead.org&gt; Cc: Andrew Morton &lt;akpm@linux-foundation.org&gt; Cc: Andrey Tsyvarev &lt;tsyvarev@ispras.ru&gt; Cc: Linus Torvalds &lt;torvalds@linux-foundation.org&gt; Cc: Paul E. McKenney &lt;paulmck@linux.vnet.ibm.com&gt; Cc: Peter Zijlstra &lt;peterz@infradead.org&gt; Cc: Rusty Russell &lt;rusty@rustcorp.com.au&gt; Cc: Thomas Gleixner &lt;tglx@linutronix.de&gt; Signed-off-by: Ingo Molnar &lt;mingo@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 35a9393c95b31870a74f51a3e7455f33f5657b6f) Signed-off-by: Mark Kuo &lt;mkuo@nvidia.com&gt;  BUG=none TEST=build and boot Smaug  Change-Id: I1333105c1c1fdeba1b6d2afe0d68e2b5b26bf85d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/303281 Commit-Ready: Mark Kuo &lt;mkuo@nvidia.com&gt; Commit-Ready: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="303281" owner_email="mkuo@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/81/303281/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1816c134e0ca33f72fff735d0aa850f4c77bcad9" commit="80bdacfae06dcf9ea2965f666bd36a32485a466c" commit_message="Uprev update_engine ebuilds to latest AOSP.  BUG=None TEST=cq  Pulled 13 new changes from platform/system/update_engine:   a59304a Merge &quot;Add metadata signature size field in payload major version 2.&quot;   b552a68 Check all signatures regardless of the version.   0532287 Transfer memory ownership when stacking ExtentWriters.   f4bb3e6 Add metadata signature size field in payload major version 2.   7599e6c update_engine: build on non-Linux hosts   e6fc8e1 Update the payload public key location in Android.   7857a55 Merge &quot;update_engine: Install payload signing public key&quot;   263614f update_engine: Install payload signing public key   cbf0989 Include the major version in update_engine.conf   2d528b4 Add unit tests to test delta performer directly.   a4365d6 Split delta performer integration test to separate file.   d78b389 Make metadata signature test independent of integration test.   af9a863 Remove obsolete Installer.* metrics.  Pulled 12 new changes from chromiumos/platform2:   1a43bce metrics: Add SendBoolToUMA to metrics interface   5daac21 minijail: Don't unmount proc if not mounted   ee5f706 buffet: Remove unnecessary calls from dbus API   46e3c8f libchromeos-ui: re-enable accelerated video decode on sandybridge.   96e7465 settingsd: Fix dbus adaptor generation.   3555036 crosh: fix error message with unknown commands   1a11d70 crosh: do not save invalid commands   460dda5 buffet: Update for libweave changes   c1f501a settingsd: implement main() function   13b93fc quipper: Update external Makefile build   559a849 buffet: Fixes for the new web server interfaces   a24c43c buffet: Update for libweave changes  Change-Id: I1816c134e0ca33f72fff735d0aa850f4c77bcad9 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/303182 Commit-Ready: Alex Deymo &lt;deymo@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Alex Deymo &lt;deymo@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Sen Jiang &lt;senj@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="303182" owner_email="deymo@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/82/303182/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="7506.0.0-rc5"/></manifest>